---
// Compass request path: one server-function entry, one scope decision, two
// storage scopes. D1 hangs off auth only, adapters hang off the impl layer.
// Two hand-tuned layouts (wide + stacked) so the mono labels stay legible
// instead of shrinking into unreadability on narrow screens.
const description =
  'Compass request flow. The browser PWA calls a single TanStack Start server function. Auth middleware binds the member scope for the request and is the only thing that touches D1, which holds Better Auth tables only. Domain implementation modules reach persistence through a store interface, which splits into two scopes: a personal scope for workouts, nutrition, coach chat and voice logs, and a household scope for finance, budget, subscriptions and shared tasks. Both scopes persist domain data to R2 as daily JSON. Adapters for Grok, SimpleFIN and the Cloudflare bindings hang off the implementation layer and stay server side.'
